! mcp_bootstrap_p378.strap -- MCP printed page 378: the SYSTEM COMMAND
! package's OFFLINE command, its tail (lines 1-24: Z OFF 20, Z OFF 10,
! Z OFF 72), and the opening of the TIME CONSTANT SETUP (Z TCC, lines
! 30-49).
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_250-445.pdf PDF p.128, read at 400 dpi.  Header, READ:
! "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 22SCOMD  CARD ID WA000843  DIST. OF 3/01
!  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 378"; the heading row's LOCATION field is 235454,
! line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  49 lines, every line number prints a "*"; a "*" after the
! LOCATION on lines 9, 31 and 48.  Contiguous 235454.00 .. 235510.40
! (line 49, a half word; next 235511.00).  Still SCOMD: no PUNID, no
! SLC, card series WA throughout.  No TAIL.
!   lines  1-24  ,.32 (the third word of p.377's B,DMCP / ,SKOM call),
!                B,ZOFF72, Z OFF 20 (C1100 IPL-mode test), Z OFF 10
!                (LI/CM mode bits), Z OFF 72 (BZBZ tapes-assigned test,
!                two ZCOM90/ZDSN01 linkages, CM1111 SPPBT1).
!   lines 25-29  remarks (banner "TIME CONSTANT SETUP" on 27).
!   lines 30-49  Z TCC .. Z TCC 01 (L(BU,26),$TC -GET TIME) .. Z TCC 02.
!
! JOIN.  p.377 ends with ,SKOM at 235453.40, a half word, so line 1's
! 235454.00 continues it; p.361's B,ZTCC prints 235473.50 = line 30.
! p.379 (Vision reading) opens at 235511.00 = line 49 + one half word.
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * "ZCFF72" (lines 2, 16) = ZOFF72; "Z CFF 10" (line 11) = ZOFF10,
!     as the ZOFF family of p.377 (open O; line 3 and 7 print Z OFF
!     closed).  Line 2's B prints 235466.10 = line 16's location.
!   * "C11CO" (line 6) = C1100: open rounds in a connective code are 0.
!   * "CMOCOO" (line 13) = CM0000; "CTICO10"/"CTIC010" = CTI0010.
!   * "LVI,O,YC1C" (line 4): the index field is a number, 0; the j
!     nibble compiles 0.
!   * "SV,C,J RET A" (line 5): C in a numeric operand is 0, as landed
!     p.199 ("SV,C," / "SX,C,"); the j nibble compiles 0 (.41).
!   * "Z CCM 90" (line 17) = ZCOM90 (lines 8, 20 print Z COM 90).
!   * >>> LINE 35 PRINTS "JCN" AND IT IS JON. <<<  The binary 000324 =
!     0o324 = 212 = JSR+JJ4+JNV+JON (4+16+64+128); p.363's JCN (1024)
!     would compile 002124.  The open glyph is this drum's open O, so the
!     deck spells it JON.  Settled by the printed binary, not the ink.
!   * "ZTCCO1"/"Z TCC 01": digit 0 (numbered family ZTCC01/02/03).
!   * hex bytes "C0"/"CO" on B rows = 00 (lesson 6; lines 9, 18, 41).
!   * line 42 prints "L(BU,26),$TC -GET TIME": the remark follows the
!     statement after one blank.
!
! CARD SERIALS.  WA000843 .. WA000887, one per line, except four
! shared: WA000850 (lines 8, 9), WA000858 (17, 18), WA000860 (20, 21),
! WA000886 (47, 48) -- each a SIC/B linkage pair.  Recorded.

